# Project rules: Quickshell Dynamic Island

## Project
A Dynamic Island / notch for Linux Wayland, built with Quickshell (Qt6 / QML) using wlr-layer-shell.
Reference apps for look and features: Alcove (macOS), NotchNook, NotchX-style notch apps.
The phased plan lives in ISLAND_PROMPT_PHASES.md. Work one phase at a time and stop at the end of each phase.

## Stack (strict)
- Quickshell + QML (Qt 6). No Tauri, React, Electron, Node, or web tech.
- Allowed helpers: small shell commands via Quickshell.Io `Process` (brightnessctl, khal, etc.).
- Do not add Python/C++ unless I explicitly ask.

## Structure
- Entry point: island/shell.qml (ShellRoot). Run with `qs -p ./island`.
- island/Island.qml (window + state), IslandShape.qml, Theme.qml (singleton), components/, services/.
- One component per file, PascalCase filenames. Register singletons in qmldir.

## Window rules
- Use PanelWindow (not ShellWindow). Anchor with `anchors { top: true }`.
- Transparent background, `exclusionMode: ExclusionMode.Ignore`, layer Overlay, namespace "island".
- The layer surface has a FIXED size (max expanded size + overshoot margin). Never resize it during animation.
- Input: `mask: Region { item: hitbox }` tracking the island's current rect. The idle notch must stay inside the mask. Everything outside is click-through.
- Keyboard focus only in "hotkey" mode (OnDemand), otherwise None.

## State rules
- `triggerMode` is one of "closed" | "hover" | "hotkey". Default "closed".
- hover enter: closed -> hover. hover exit: hover -> closed after a 150 ms debounce. Hotkey mode ignores exit.
- toggleHotkey(): closed/hover -> hotkey; hotkey -> closed. Escape also closes hotkey mode.
- Hotkey must be reachable two ways: GlobalShortcut (Hyprland) and IpcHandler `qs ipc call island toggle`.
- Activities (media, battery, timer, HUD, notification) are a separate `activity` property and must never override a locked hotkey state.

## Visual rules
- Shape is a custom `QtQuick.Shapes` path: flush top edge, concave flares at top corners, convex rounded bottom corners. Never a plain Rectangle.
- Fill #000000, no border. Sizes live in Theme.qml (idle 200x34, hover 360x80, expanded 640x220).
- Motion: SpringAnimation on width/height/bottomRadius (default spring 3.5, damping 0.35, epsilon 0.25). Tunables live in Theme.qml.
- Content fades in after the shape grows and is disabled when invisible.

## Code conventions
- Colors, sizes, durations, spring values come from Theme.qml. No magic numbers in components.
- Prefer declarative bindings over imperative JS. Keep JS functions small.
- Services are thin wrappers around Quickshell.Services.* and expose simple properties.
- Degrade gracefully when an optional tool is missing (khal, brightnessctl): hide the feature, never crash.
- No polling faster than needed. When closed and idle, no running timers or animations.

## Workflow
- Before deleting files, list them and wait for my "confirm".
- After each change run `qmllint` on touched files and `qs -p ./island` to check for load errors; report any errors.
- Do not invent Quickshell APIs. If unsure a type or property exists, check the Quickshell docs/source and tell me what you verified.
- Keep README.md updated with run instructions and hotkey binds for Hyprland and other compositors.
- Make small, reviewable commits per phase. Do not refactor unrelated files.
- When a requirement conflicts with these rules, stop and ask.
